{
  "description": "std-record-detail — single primitive: detail-panel. Owns the fetch-one-record state machine (loading → viewing → error, with RETRY), the record counterpart to std-browse's collection machine. Consumers configure fields/sections/actions and the title/subtitle/status bindings; the atom fetches by the id carried on INIT and renders the panel. `detailLook` (panel default / slide-over / page) selects one of three render bodies. Pair with std-detail-layout for the back + breadcrumb chrome — that atom owns navigation, this one owns the record — exactly as a list page pairs std-browse with std-app-layout.",
